1.3 Bob Jenkins, lookup3

Yices uses hash functions from Bob Jenkins' lookup3 code. The implementations
are in src/utils/hash_functions.c and src/utils/hash_functions.h, and derived
hash codes appear in a number of other files, including
src/solvers/egraph/composites.c, src/utils/cache.c,
src/utils/pair_hash_map.c, src/utils/pair_hash_sets.c, src/utils/ptr_sets.c,
src/solvers/bv/bvsolver.c, src/solvers/simplex/arith_atomtable.c, and
src/solvers/egraph/egraph_eq_stats.c.

Bob Jenkins placed lookup3 in the public domain. The Yices sources record this
where the code is used, and give http://www.burtleburtle.net as the source.

1.4 Timsort

src/utils/stable_sort.h and src/utils/stable_sort.c implement a stable sort.
The header records that the implementation is based on Tim Peters' timsort, as
used by Python, with the galloping part omitted, and cites two references: the
timsort description at http://bugs.python.org/file4451/timsort.txt and the
CPython file Objects/listobject.c.

The status of this material is unresolved. The cited references cover both an
algorithm description and a specific implementation, and the Yices sources do
not record which of the two the code follows. This notice records the
attribution the sources give. It does not resolve the question, and readers
should not treat the absence of a further notice here as a determination
either way.


