the binary archives carry. That file names the compiler the build used and the
first line of its version output, and it identifies the C library the binaries
were built against. Where the build links a C library archive, it gives that
archive's checksum and names the source package the archive came from. It also
gives the GMP version, the LibPoly source revision, and for each of those two
components the file name and checksum of the source asset published with this
release.

Section 6. Materials for rebuilding
------------------------------------

Some of the libraries built into the Yices binaries are distributed under
terms that give you the right to modify them and rebuild Yices against your
modified version. The material needed to do that is published as a separate
asset alongside the binary archives, together with the corresponding library
source.

You do not need any of it to install or run Yices. If you only want to use
Yices, the ordinary distribution archive is complete on its own.
